.TITLE "mkdir"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Creates new directories on macOS. This command allows users to create one or
more directories at specified paths. It is a fundamental utility for
__filesystem management__ and organizing files. Options are available
for creating parent directories as needed and setting permissions.

.DIV "ALIAS"
**makedir**

.DIV "TLDR"
**mkdir __new_directory__**
Creates a single new directory named __new_directory__ in the current location.
> __new_directory__: The name of the directory to create.

**mkdir -p __parent_dir/new_directory__**
Creates __new_directory__ and any necessary parent directories.
> __-p__: parents flag | __parent_dir/new_directory__: The path to the new directory, including parents.

**mkdir __dir1__ __dir2__**
Creates multiple directories (__dir1__, __dir2__) simultaneously.
> __dir1__: Name of the first directory. | __dir2__: Name of the second directory.

**mkdir -m __755__ __permissions_dir__**
Creates a directory named __permissions_dir__ with specific octal __755__ permissions.
> __-m__: mode flag | __755__: The octal representation of file permissions. | __permissions_dir__: The name of the directory to create.

.DIV "SUMMARY"
`mkdir -p` is particularly useful for creating nested directory structures
without needing to create each parent directory individually. Ensure you have
write permissions in the parent directory where you intend to create new ones.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:rm** **mac:mv**

documentation: https://ss64.com/osx/mkdir.html
